= Define Our Ideology

The party stands for many things. Voters, donors, and activists want a clear answer about what we are.

- @progressive_turn: A bolder, progressive agenda
- @pragmatic_center: Pragmatic center
- @abundance_agenda: The abundance agenda
- @populist_economics: Economic populism
- @easy_discard

@progressive_turn
on-arrival: progressive_strength += 6; moderate_strength -= 2; establishment_strength -= 2; progressive_dissent -= 8; moderate_dissent += 6; biz_relation -= 4; left_relation += 4; farleft_strength -= 0.5; young_dem += 3*(1-dissent); suburban_dem -= 2*(1-dissent); month_actions += 1

We champion universal programs and confront concentrated wealth. The left feels heard; swing voters watch nervously.

@pragmatic_center
on-arrival: moderate_strength += 5; establishment_strength += 2; progressive_strength -= 4; progressive_dissent += 6; moderate_dissent -= 5; suburban_dem += 4*(1-dissent); biz_relation += 4; left_relation -= 5; farleft_strength += 0.6; month_actions += 1

We emphasize competence and bipartisan achievements. Moderates breathe easier; activists wonder where the fight went.

@abundance_agenda
on-arrival: abundance_discovered = 1; abundance_strength += 6; progressive_dissent += 2; labor_dissent += 1; suburban_dem += 2*(1-dissent); young_dem += 2*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 0.2; month_actions += 1

Build more housing, clean energy, and transit; make government deliver. The agenda draws new energy and some skepticism from those wary of deregulation.

@populist_economics
on-arrival: populist_discovered = 1; populist_strength += 6; labor_strength += 2; working_dem += 4*(1-dissent); rural_dem += 2*(1-dissent); educated_dem -= 2*(1-dissent); abundance_dissent += 3; progressive_dissent += 2; month_actions += 1

We take on monopolies, trade deals, and corporate power with a message aimed at working families of every background.
